  "strategy": "4. Search choices and useful variations\n- Parameter bounds: param1(range:0.0-2.0), param2(range:-1.0-1.0), basis_scale(range:1.0-10.0), resolution(range:1-10)\n- Uses probability-based initialization\n- Includes probabilistic basis terms with adaptive resolution\n- The Bayesian optimization phase establishes a good starting point for local search\n- Time-adaptive grid selection ensures optimal performance given budget constraints\n- Combines parametric search with period-based optimization\n\n5. Compute budget and robustness\n- Basis optimization: O(budget_factor) function evaluations\n- Bayesian optimization: Limited by the init_points and n_iter\n- Local search: Bounded by dimensionality \n- Time estimations: 50% of budget for Bayesian, 40% for local search, 10% for final polish\n- Fallback: Returns n_points=140 for tight budgets\n- Robustness: Full bounds checking, continuous removal, and repair operations\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n- Verifies integral constraint: sum(h)*dx must be approximately 1\n- Confirms function bounds: 0<=h[i]<=1 for all i\n- Includes continuity check for the basis functions\n- Returns the C5 value computed using the evaluate_erdos_solution function\n- Includes fallback solution if time constraint exceeded\n\nThe implementation delivers a parameterized basis approach optimized through Bayesian and gradient-based methods, designed to outperform previous solutions while respecting the computational budget constraints.",
